  "notes": "A formal word used mainly in legislative, judicial, and administrative contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {審議|しんぎ}する: to deliberate\n- {審議|しんぎ}に{入|はい}る: to enter deliberation\n- {審議|しんぎ}{中|ちゅう}: under deliberation\n- {審議|しんぎ}を{尽|つ}くす: to deliberate thoroughly\n- {審議|しんぎ}{会|かい}: deliberation council\n\nWATCH OUT:\n{真偽|しんぎ} (truth or falsehood) is pronounced the same but has a completely different meaning.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {審議|しんぎ}: formal deliberation (legislature, committee)\n- {議論|ぎろん}: discussion, debate (general)\n- {検討|けんとう}: examination, consideration (less formal)",
